### 8.1 Common states

Don't express every combination with a single enum of state. Define interaction (default/hover/pressed/focus-visible), availability (enabled/disabled), async (idle/loading/success/error) and selection (unselected/selected) as orthogonal axes. The priority is disabled → loading action limits → invalid/selected meaning → interaction, and focus-visible stays together with the meaning indicator while keyboard focus is present.

| Component | States that must be defined | Behavior contract |
|---|---|---|
| Button | default, hover, pressed, focus-visible, disabled, loading | type defaults to button. Block duplicate runs while loading; keep label and width |
| Field/TextInput | empty, filled, hover, focus, invalid, disabled, readOnly | Connect label, connect description and error ids, aria-invalid when invalid |
| Combobox | closed, open, filtering, no-result, selected, error | Search, Arrow to move, Enter to select, Esc to close, loading indicator |
| Tabs | selected, focus-visible, disabled | WAI-ARIA tabs pattern, Arrow to move, aria-controls connected |
| Dialog/Drawer | closed, open, submitting, error | Name and description, focus move · trap · return, disable the background |
| Table | loading, data, empty, filtered-empty, error, selected | Real table semantic structure, sort button and aria-sort, bulk selection |
| Upload | idle, dragover, validating, uploading, paused, complete, error, canceled | Provide a choose button, real progress, per-item retry on failure |
| AsyncJob | queued, running, succeeded, failed, canceling, canceled | Transition only on confirmed backend states; state retry conditions and cancel results |

Button variants: primary / secondary / ghost / danger. sizes: sm (32px, dense secondary actions only), md (40px), lg (48px). Secure 44px or more for touch UI. icon-only requires an accessibleName; async loading uses aria-busy and a status announcement. Don't use sm for a primary CTA.

disabled blocks the action with HTML disabled. Give the reason for being disabled in nearby text, not only in a hover tooltip. When focus must be preserved during loading, mark it with aria-disabled and block both click and keyboard events. Don't disable an input just because of an error the user can fix.

Forms validate on blur or submit, and afterward clear errors as the input changes. On a failed submit, provide an error summary and a way to jump to the first invalid field. A placeholder doesn't replace a label. Distinguish readOnly from disabled both visually and in behavior.

Tooltip is for explanation and holds no required information or interactive content. Content that must be operated by click or keyboard moves to a Popover. Toast is for secondary confirmation, and important failures stay in the body as an Alert. For menu and dialog focus, Esc and nesting behavior, use the verified patterns of accessibility primitives. Component tone system: Badge, Alert, Toast and Dialog icons use four tones — neutral, success, warning and error — composed in the stages of surface (status surface), border (status border), icon/dot and text. Every color is chosen within the orange, charcoal, warm-gray and white palette: a success badge is a charcoal fill, an error badge is an orange fill, and a warning badge is a light orange outline. Toast and Tooltip use bg.inverse and text.inverse, so in dark mode they flip to a light surface. Dialog has a head (icon · title · description · close), a body and a foot (canvas surface, cancel → primary action); an irreversible action like delete uses an error-tone icon and a charcoal (white in dark) button, with focus on Cancel. Checkboxes, radios, switches, progress and selected tabs use #FD4D20 only for the selected state.

### 8.2 Button API example

```ts
type ButtonProps = {
  variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary' | 'ghost' | 'danger';
  size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg';
  loading?: boolean;
  disabled?: boolean;
  type?: 'button' | 'submit' | 'reset';
  onClick?: React.MouseEventHandler<HTMLButtonElement>;
  children: React.ReactNode;
};
// Provide links as a separate Link component. Don't fake URL navigation with onClick.
// Compose native button attributes and ref forwarding without conflicts in the real implementation.
```

Reproduce each variant's color, every state, line wrapping, icons and submit behavior in Storybook or an equivalent example environment. In the implementation, block icon-only buttons missing an accessible name with lint or tests.

The following is a structural example. Final code is generated from the token source; do not manage the CSS below as a separate source. Spacing token names use the px value directly (`--hds-space-16` = 16px = 1rem).

```css
:root {
  --hds-color-orange-500: #fd4d20;
  --hds-color-orange-700: #b34202;
  --hds-color-warm-0: #fff;
  --hds-color-warm-50: #faf9f6;
  --hds-color-warm-950: #171614;
  --hds-bg-canvas: var(--hds-color-warm-50);
  --hds-bg-surface: var(--hds-color-warm-0);
  --hds-text-primary: var(--hds-color-warm-950);
  --hds-action-primary-bg: var(--hds-color-orange-500);
  --hds-action-primary-fg: var(--hds-color-warm-950);
  --hds-space-16: 1rem;   /* name = px value */
  --hds-space-24: 1.5rem;
  --hds-space-32: 2rem;
  --hds-radius-control: .5rem;
  --hds-font-body-md: 1rem;
  --hds-line-body-md: 1.6;
}
html { font-size: 100%; }
body { color: var(--hds-text-primary); background: var(--hds-bg-canvas); }
.docs-shell {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 15rem minmax(0, 1fr) 12rem;
  gap: var(--hds-space-32);
  max-width: 90rem;
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding-inline: var(--hds-space-32);
}
.docs-main { min-width: 0; }
.prose { max-width: 68ch; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.code-scroll { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; }
.button {
  min-height: 2.5rem;
  padding: .625rem 1rem;
  border-radius: var(--hds-radius-control);
  white-space: normal;
}
.button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 2px; }
@media (max-width: 79.999rem) {
  .docs-shell { grid-template-columns: 14rem minmax(0, 1fr); }
  /* Move the right-hand table of contents into a collapsible TOC above the content. Do not simply delete it. */
}
@media (max-width: 63.999rem) {
  .docs-shell { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); padding-inline: var(--hds-space-24); }
  /* Switch the left navigation to an accessible Drawer. */
}
@media (max-width: 47.999rem) {
  .docs-shell { padding-inline: var(--hds-space-16); }
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .motion-element { transition-duration: 0ms; animation: none; }
}
```

Implement media-query switches together with DOM and accessibility state changes. Do not merely hide with CSS, which makes the same navigation read twice or leaves focus off-screen. Spacing in rem follows the user's font setting, while borders and the like may stay in px.
